				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				740,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Reduce stderr spam from extension handler errors\n\nDowngrade error logging for extension-provided handlers ($provide*, $resolve*,\n$get*) from console.error (full stack trace) to console.warn (single-line message).\n\nWhen extension handlers throw errors, the full stack trace was being dumped to\nstderr, causing Mountain to emit `warn: Cocoon stderr` spam—even though the\nfault lies in the extension's code, not Cocoon itself. The IPC response still\ncarries the error payload back to the caller, so error information is not lost.\n\nRouteManifest regenerated with updated timestamps.",
			"SHA": "7e224b6335bee89b92711a438047e63f4c99d35a"
		},
